              <span class="about-paper-role">Local decision surfaces</span>
              <span class="about-paper-nick">LAMP</span>
            </div>
            <div class="about-paper-title">Extracting Local Decision Surfaces From Large Language Models</div>
            <p class="about-paper-blurb">
              Fluent LLM explanations need not track what actually drives the prediction. LAMP treats the model’s own stated factors as coordinates
              and fits a local linear decision surface—without gradients or internal access—to test whether predictions move consistently when those
              factors change.
            </p>
            <div class="about-paper-venue"><span class="about-spotlight">Spotlight paper</span> in AISTATS 2026</div>
